 that do not appear above are those that appear in the dominant lists at later cooling time. Pathways are retained if they contribute more than the path floor
 percentage of the number of target  atoms given by the rate equation solution for the time interval. Loops are retained in a pathway if they contribute more
 than the loop floor percentage of the number of target atoms created along the pathway.
